<title>USA: Ahmanson improves offer for Great Western.</title>
<headline>Ahmanson improves offer for Great Western.</headline>
<dateline>IRWINDALE, Calif. 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>H.F. Ahmanson &amp; Co said Monday it enhanced its proposal to acquire Great Western Financial Corp by merger, in an offer that it said was superior to a rival bid by Washington Mutual Savings Bank.</p>
<p>Ahmanson said that based on the closing price of Washington Mutual shares and Ahmanson shares on March 14, its improved offer provides a premium of $400 million or about $3 a share over the implied value by the Washington Mutual proposal.</p>
</text>
